**DPC Impact Hub**

Full System Scope & Design Specification

Graeme Wright  ·  Digital Pedagogy Coach  ·  Quality & Innovation  ·  Weston College Group  ·  June 2026

Version 1.0  ·  Living document — updated as the system evolves

*This document captures the full intended scope of the DPC Impact Hub: what it does, what it will do, how the pieces connect, and the design thinking behind the connective wiring. It is both a specification and a record of the design conversations that shaped it.*

**1.  Purpose ****&**** Philosophy**

The DPC Impact Hub is the personal operating system for the Digital Pedagogy Coach role at Weston College Group. It is not an IT system, a compliance tool, or a tracking spreadsheet. It is a coaching intelligence platform — designed to capture evidence of practice, support structured professional conversations, close the loop between observation and improvement, and produce meaningful reports for different audiences.

**Core principles**

- Digital supports and enhances exceptional TLA practice. It does not replace it.

- Evidence must be genuine — only real, completed activity is recorded or reported.

- Coaching without authority — influence through relational capital, not hierarchy.

- Accessibility is non-negotiable throughout — WCAG 2.2 AA minimum on all outputs.

- The system serves the coach, not the other way around. Capture should be fast; insight should be rich.

- Closing the loop is the point. An observation without a follow-through is data without meaning.

**Strategic framework**

All activity maps to the Digital Learning Pyramid: Digital Foundations (Level 1) → Digital Inclusion (Level 2) → Digital Innovation (Level 3). Learning Without Barriers runs through all three levels as a non-negotiable thread. External frameworks referenced: ETF DTPF, DigCompEdu, Jisc Building Digital Capability Discovery Tool, UDL (CAST), Quality First Teaching.

**Architecture**

Local-first, browser-based single-page application. Data stored in localStorage with manual JSON download as backup. Hosted on GitHub Pages (gwc25/dpc-impact-hub). No server, no IT dependency, no individual logins required. Password-protected at entry. WCAG 2.2 AA throughout.

**2.  The Data Model**

Everything in the Hub shares one data store: DPC.DB. All modules read from and write to this single JSON object. The join key across all records is the three-letter area code (e.g. BUI, CON, HBH). This is non-negotiable — area code standardisation is the single most important data integrity action across the whole system.

**Core data objects**

| **DPC.DB.areas[]** | 35 curriculum areas. Each carries: RAG ratings, health check scores, activity log, interventions, staff development records, action points, current actions, Digital Lead identity, HoA identity. |
| --- | --- |
| **DPC.DB.staffProfiles[]** | Individual staff records — created dynamically when first encountered via DevObs, LW, referral or coaching. Not pre-populated. See Section 6. |
| **DPC.DB.individualActivities[]** | Cross-college or non-area activities — DPC CPD, external events, strategic meetings. |
| **DPC.DB.myCPD[]** | DPC personal CPD log with post-impact confidence ratings. |
| **DPC.DB.templates[]** | Teach meet plans, coaching question sets, meeting agenda templates, observation frameworks. Reusable across contexts. |
| **DPC.DB.reflections[]** | Anonymous reflections from staff following coaching, teach meets, CPD. Tagged to event and area. Named at individual profile level, anonymous at area level. |
| **DPC.DB.afiRecords[]** | First-class AFI objects with full lifecycle — see Section 7. |

